/-!
# Descent of standard syntomic algebras

Let `K / k` be a field extension and `A` a `k`-algebra. If `K ⊗[k] A` is locally standard syntomic
of relative dimension `n` over `K`, then `A` is locally standard syntomic of relative dimension `n`
over `k` (`TauCeti.locally_isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_of_tensorProduct`). In other
words, being a local complete intersection of relative dimension `n` over a field is insensitive
to extending the field.

Combined with the fibrewise criterion
`TauCeti.locally_isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_of_fiber`, this gives descent along every
faithfully flat ring map `R → S`
(`TauCeti.codescendsAlong_locally_isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_faithfullyFlat`):
flatness and finite presentation descend, and the fibre of `S ⊗[R] T` over a prime of `S` is the
base change of the fibre of `T` along an extension of residue fields. This is the affine input
for fpqc descent of syntomic morphisms of schemes.

Being a local complete intersection over a field also descends along étale maps of the source.
If `A` is of finite type over `k` and `B` is an étale `A`-algebra which is locally standard
syntomic of relative dimension `n` over `k`, then every prime of `A` under a prime of `B` has a
standard syntomic neighbourhood
(`TauCeti.exists_notMem_isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_localization_away_of_etale`). This
is the affine input for descending syntomicity, and with it nodality of relative curves, along
étale covers of the source.

The proofs bound the number of equations needed near a prime `q` of `A`. Present `A` as
`k[x₁, …, x_m] ⧸ I`. Near a prime `q'` of `K ⊗[k] A` over `q`, the algebra `K ⊗[k] A` has a
standard syntomic chart `(K ⊗[k] A)[1/t] = K[z₁, …, z_{n+c}] ⧸ (f₁, …, f_c)`. Comparing this
presentation with the presentation of `(K ⊗[k] A)[1/t]` by the generators `x` and one more
generator inverting `t` (`Algebra.Generators.finrank_tensor_cotangent_add_card_le`,
`Algebra.Generators.finrank_tensor_cotangent_comp_localizationAway`) bounds the dimension of the
fibre of the extended ideal `I K[x]` at `q'` by `m - n`. As `K[x]` is flat over `k[x]`, this is
also the dimension of the fibre of `I` (`Ideal.finrank_tensor_map_of_flat`). By Nakayama's lemma
(`Module.exists_finset_card_le_finrank_and_smul_mem_span`), after inverting some `g ∉ q` the
ideal `I` is generated by `d ≤ m - n` elements, which presents `A[1/g]` by `m + 1` generators and
`d + 1` relations. Since `dim A = dim (K ⊗[k] A) ≤ n`, Krull's height theorem forces `d = m - n`
and shows that `A[1/g]` has dimension `n`
(`TauCeti.exists_notMem_isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_localization_away_of_finrank_le`).

In the étale case, shrink `B` around a prime `Q` over `q` until it is standard étale over `A`, with
presentation `A[y, w] ⧸ (f, w g - 1)`, and standard syntomic over `k`. Presenting `B` over `k` by
the generators `x, y, w`, the fibre of the conormal module at `Q` has dimension two more than that
of `I` (`Algebra.Generators.finrank_tensor_cotangent_comp_of_isStandardEtale`), and comparison with
the standard syntomic presentation of `B` again bounds the fibre of `I` by `m - n`. The image of
`Spec B → Spec A` is an open neighbourhood of `q`, and on it heights are at most
`dim B ≤ n`, since flat maps satisfy going down.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.exists_notMem_isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_localization_away_of_tensorProduct`:
  every prime `q` of `A` has a standard syntomic neighbourhood `A[1/g]`, `g ∉ q`, of relative
  dimension `n` over `k`.
* `TauCeti.locally_isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_of_tensorProduct`: `A` is locally
  standard syntomic of relative dimension `n` over `k`.
* `TauCeti.codescendsAlong_locally_isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_faithfullyFlat`: locally
  standard syntomic ring maps of relative dimension `n` descend along faithfully flat ring maps.
* `TauCeti.exists_notMem_isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_localization_away_of_finrank_le`: a
  presentation whose kernel has a small fibre at a point, near which heights are at most `n`, gives
  a standard syntomic neighbourhood of that point.
* `TauCeti.exists_notMem_isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_localization_away_of_etale`: every
  prime of `A` under a prime of an étale, locally standard syntomic `A`-algebra has a standard
  syntomic neighbourhood.
* `TauCeti.locally_isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_of_etale`: local complete intersections
  over a field descend along faithfully flat étale maps.

## References

* The Stacks Project, Commutative Algebra, Section *Syntomic morphisms*: being a local complete
  intersection over a field is unchanged by extending the field, and a presentation whose kernel
  needs the expected number of generators near a prime is a relative global complete
  intersection near that prime.
* The Stacks Project, Descent, Section *Properties of morphisms local in the syntomic topology on
  the source*: syntomicity is local on the source for the syntomic, hence the étale, topology.
-/

public section

open TensorProduct

namespace TauCeti

universe u

variable {n : ℕ} {k K A : Type u} [Field k] [Field K] [Algebra k K] [CommRing A] [Algebra k A]

attribute [local instance] MvPolynomial.algebraMvPolynomial

/-- Let `P` present `A` over `k` with generators indexed by `ι`, and let `q` be a prime of `A`. If
`K ⊗[k] A` is locally standard syntomic of relative dimension `n`, then at some field-valued point
`F` of `k[ι]` lying over `q`, the fibre of the kernel of `P` has dimension at most `#ι - n`. -/
private theorem exists_finrank_tensor_ker_add_le {ι σ : Type} [Finite ι] [Finite σ]
    (P : Algebra.Presentation k A ι σ)
    (h : RingHom.Locally (IsStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension n) (algebraMap K (K ⊗[k] A)))
    (q : Ideal A) [q.IsPrime] :
    ∃ (F : Type u) (_ : Field F) (_ : Algebra P.Ring F),
      (∀ r : P.Ring, algebraMap P.Ring A r ∈ q → algebraMap P.Ring F r = 0) ∧
      Module.finrank F (F ⊗[P.Ring] P.ker) + n ≤ Nat.card ι := by
  -- A prime `q'` of `K ⊗[k] A` over `q`.
  obtain ⟨q₁, hq₁⟩ := PrimeSpectrum.comap_surjective_of_faithfullyFlat (A := A) (B := A ⊗[k] K)
    ⟨q, inferInstance⟩
  let q' : Ideal (K ⊗[k] A) := q₁.asIdeal.comap (Algebra.TensorProduct.comm k K A).toRingHom
  have hq' : q'.comap Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight.toRingHom = q := by
    rw [Ideal.comap_comap]
    convert congrArg PrimeSpectrum.asIdeal hq₁ using 2
    ext a
    simp
  -- A standard syntomic chart `T = (K ⊗[k] A)[1/t]` around `q'`.
  obtain ⟨s, hs, hst⟩ := h
  have hq'top : q' ≠ ⊤ := fun h ↦ ‹q.IsPrime›.ne_top (by rw [← hq', h, Ideal.comap_top])
  obtain ⟨t, hts, hdisj⟩ := Ideal.exists_disjoint_powers_of_span_eq_top s hs q' hq'top
  let T := Localization.Away t
  have hT : Algebra.IsStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension n K T := by
    rw [← isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_algebraMap,
      IsScalarTower.algebraMap_eq K (K ⊗[k] A)]
    exact hst t hts
  let Q := q'.map (algebraMap (K ⊗[k] A) T)
  have : Q.IsPrime := IsLocalization.isPrime_of_isPrime_disjoint _ _ q' inferInstance hdisj.symm
  -- The point `F = κ(Q)`, with its algebra structures over `K ⊗[k] A`, `K[ι]` and `k[ι]`.
  let F := Q.ResidueField
  let PK := P.baseChange K
  let : Algebra (K ⊗[k] A) F := ((algebraMap T F).comp (algebraMap (K ⊗[k] A) T)).toAlgebra
  let : Algebra PK.Ring F :=
    ((algebraMap (K ⊗[k] A) F).comp (algebraMap PK.Ring (K ⊗[k] A))).toAlgebra
  let : Algebra P.Ring F := ((algebraMap PK.Ring F).comp (algebraMap P.Ring PK.Ring)).toAlgebra
  have : IsScalarTower (K ⊗[k] A) T F := .of_algebraMap_eq' rfl
  have : IsScalarTower PK.Ring (K ⊗[k] A) F := .of_algebraMap_eq' rfl
  have : IsScalarTower P.Ring PK.Ring F := .of_algebraMap_eq' rfl
  refine ⟨F, inferInstance, inferInstance, fun r hr ↦ ?_, ?_⟩
  · have hr' : algebraMap PK.Ring (K ⊗[k] A) (algebraMap P.Ring PK.Ring r) =
        Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight (algebraMap P.Ring A r) :=
      P.toGenerators.algebraMap_baseChange_map K r
    rw [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply P.Ring PK.Ring F,
      IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply PK.Ring (K ⊗[k] A) F,
      IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply (K ⊗[k] A) T F, hr', Ideal.algebraMap_residueField_eq_zero]
    refine Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ?_
    rw [← hq'] at hr
    exact hr
  · obtain ⟨ι', σ', _, _, P', hP'⟩ := hT.exists_presentation
    -- The kernel of `K[ι] → K ⊗[k] A` is the extension of the kernel of `k[ι] → A`.
    have hker := P.ker_baseChange_eq_map K
    have : Module.Flat P.Ring PK.Ring :=
      Module.Flat.isBaseChange (R := k) (M := K) _ _ (Algebra.IsPushout.out (R := k) (S := P.Ring)
        (R' := K) (S' := PK.Ring))
    have : Module.Finite (K ⊗[k] A) PK.toExtension.Cotangent :=
      Algebra.Extension.Cotangent.finite PK.fg_ker
    have h1 := ((Algebra.Generators.localizationAway T t).comp
      PK.toGenerators).finrank_tensor_cotangent_add_card_le F P'
    rw [Algebra.Generators.finrank_tensor_cotangent_comp_localizationAway,
      Algebra.Generators.finrank_tensor_cotangent, hker, Ideal.finrank_tensor_map_of_flat] at h1
    simp only [Nat.card_sum, Nat.card_unique, hP'] at h1
    omega

/-- If every prime of `A` avoiding `a` has height at most `n`, then so does every prime of
`A[1/(c a)]`. -/
private theorem ringKrullDim_localization_away_mul_le {a : A}
    (hdim : ∀ p : Ideal A, p.IsPrime → a ∉ p → Ideal.height p ≤ n) (c : A) :
    ringKrullDim (Localization.Away (c * a)) ≤ n := by
  refine (ringKrullDim_le_iff_height_le _).mpr fun p _ ↦ ?_
  rw [← IsLocalization.height_under (Submonoid.powers (c * a)) p]
  -- The prime of `A` under `p` avoids `c a`, hence avoids `a`.
  refine WithBot.coe_le_coe.mpr (hdim (p.under A) inferInstance fun ha ↦ ?_)
  have hunit := IsLocalization.Away.algebraMap_isUnit (S := Localization.Away (c * a)) (c * a)
  exact ‹p.IsPrime›.ne_top
    (p.eq_top_of_isUnit_mem (Ideal.mem_comap.mp (Ideal.mul_mem_left (p.under A) c ha)) hunit)

/-- **A presentation criterion for standard syntomic charts.** Let `P` present a `k`-algebra `A`
with generators indexed by `ι`, and let `q` be a prime of `A`. Suppose that at a field-valued point
`F` of `k[ι]` lying over `q` the fibre of the kernel of `P` has dimension at most `#ι - n`, and that
every prime of `A` avoiding some `a ∉ q` has height at most `n`. Then `q` has a neighbourhood
`A[1/g]`, `g ∉ q`, which is standard syntomic of relative dimension `n` over `k`. -/
theorem exists_notMem_isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_localization_away_of_finrank_le
    {ι σ : Type*} [Finite ι] [Finite σ] (P : Algebra.Presentation k A ι σ) (q : Ideal A)
    [q.IsPrime] (F : Type*) [Field F] [Algebra P.Ring F]
    (hF : ∀ r : P.Ring, algebraMap P.Ring A r ∈ q → algebraMap P.Ring F r = 0)
    (hfin : Module.finrank F (F ⊗[P.Ring] P.ker) + n ≤ Nat.card ι) {a : A} (ha : a ∉ q)
    (hdim : ∀ p : Ideal A, p.IsPrime → a ∉ p → Ideal.height p ≤ n) :
    ∃ g ∉ q, Algebra.IsStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension n k (Localization.Away g) := by
  classical
  have : Module.Finite P.Ring P.ker := by
    rw [Module.Finite.iff_fg, ← P.span_range_relation_eq_ker]
    exact Submodule.fg_span (Set.finite_range _)
  -- By Nakayama's lemma, after inverting some `r` the kernel needs at most `#ι - n` generators.
  obtain ⟨s, hs, r, hr, hrs⟩ :=
    Module.exists_finset_card_le_finrank_and_smul_mem_span (R := P.Ring) (M := P.ker) (F := F)
  let ϕ : P.Ring →ₐ[k] A := MvPolynomial.aeval P.val
  have hker : RingHom.ker ϕ = P.ker := P.ker_eq_ker_aeval_val.symm
  have hk : ∀ l : s, (l : P.ker).val ∈ RingHom.ker ϕ := fun l ↦ by
    rw [hker]
    exact (l : P.ker).property
  obtain ⟨b, rfl⟩ := P.aeval_val_surjective a
  have hg : ∀ x ∈ RingHom.ker ϕ,
      r * b * x ∈ Ideal.span (Set.range fun l : s ↦ (l : P.ker).val) := by
    intro x hx
    rw [hker] at hx
    have := Submodule.mem_map_of_mem (f := P.ker.subtype) (hrs ⟨x, hx⟩)
    rw [Submodule.map_span] at this
    have hrange : (Set.range fun l : s ↦ (l : P.ker).val) = P.ker.subtype '' s := by
      ext
      simp
    rw [mul_right_comm, hrange]
    exact Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ this
  obtain ⟨PB⟩ := Algebra.Presentation.nonempty_presentation_localizationAway
    P.aeval_val_surjective hk hg
  have hrq : ϕ (r * b) ∉ q := by
    rw [map_mul]
    exact ‹q.IsPrime›.mul_notMem
      (fun h' ↦ hr (hF r (by rwa [Algebra.Generators.algebraMap_apply]))) ha
  refine ⟨ϕ (r * b), hrq, ?_⟩
  -- `A[1/ϕ (r b)]` is nonzero, its primes have height at most `n`, and its presentation has at
  -- least `n` more generators than relations.
  have hdisj : Disjoint (Submonoid.powers (ϕ (r * b)) : Set A) q :=
    (Ideal.disjoint_powers_iff_notMem _ ‹q.IsPrime›.isRadical).mpr hrq
  have hqB : (q.map (algebraMap A (Localization.Away (ϕ (r * b))))).IsPrime :=
    IsLocalization.isPrime_of_isPrime_disjoint _ _ q inferInstance hdisj
  have : Nontrivial (Localization.Away (ϕ (r * b))) := nontrivial_of_ne 0 1 fun h ↦
    hqB.ne_top ((Ideal.eq_top_iff_one _).mpr (h ▸ Ideal.zero_mem _))
  refine PB.isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_of_ringKrullDim_le ?_
    (map_mul ϕ r b ▸ ringKrullDim_localization_away_mul_le hdim (ϕ r))
  have := Fintype.ofFinite ι
  simp only [Nat.card_eq_fintype_card, Fintype.card_sum, Fintype.card_unit,
    Fintype.card_coe] at hfin ⊢
  omega

/-- **Standard syntomic charts descend along field extensions.** If `K ⊗[k] A` is locally standard
syntomic of relative dimension `n` over the extension field `K`, then every prime `q` of `A` has a
neighbourhood `A[1/g]`, `g ∉ q`, which is standard syntomic of relative dimension `n` over `k`. -/
theorem exists_notMem_isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_localization_away_of_tensorProduct
    (h : RingHom.Locally (IsStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension n) (algebraMap K (K ⊗[k] A)))
    (q : Ideal A) [q.IsPrime] :
    ∃ g ∉ q, Algebra.IsStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension n k (Localization.Away g) := by
  -- `A` is finitely presented over `k`, since `K ⊗[k] A` is finitely presented over `K`.
  have : Algebra.FinitePresentation K (K ⊗[k] A) := RingHom.finitePresentation_algebraMap.mp
    (finitePresentation_of_locally_isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension h)
  have : Algebra.FinitePresentation k A := .of_finitePresentation_tensorProduct_of_faithfullyFlat K
  let P := Algebra.Presentation.ofFinitePresentation k A
  obtain ⟨F, _, _, hF, hfin⟩ := exists_finrank_tensor_ker_add_le P h q
  -- Every prime of `A` has height at most `dim A = dim (K ⊗[k] A) ≤ n`.
  have hdimA : ringKrullDim A ≤ n := by
    rw [← ringKrullDim_tensorProduct_field_of_finiteType (k := k) K A]
    exact ringKrullDim_le_of_locally_isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension h
  exact exists_notMem_isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_localization_away_of_finrank_le
    P q F hF hfin (Ideal.one_notMem q) fun p _ _ ↦
      WithBot.coe_le_coe.mp (Ideal.height_le_ringKrullDim_of_isPrime.trans hdimA)

/-- **Local complete intersections descend along field extensions.** If `K ⊗[k] A` is locally
standard syntomic of relative dimension `n` over the extension field `K`, then `A` is locally
standard syntomic of relative dimension `n` over `k`. -/
theorem locally_isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_of_tensorProduct
    (h : RingHom.Locally (IsStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension n) (algebraMap K (K ⊗[k] A))) :
    RingHom.Locally (IsStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension n) (algebraMap k A) := by
  rw [RingHom.locally_iff_span_eq_top]
  by_contra hne
  obtain ⟨m, hm, hle⟩ := Ideal.exists_le_maximal _ hne
  obtain ⟨g, hg, hstd⟩ :=
    exists_notMem_isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_localization_away_of_tensorProduct h m
  refine hg (hle (Ideal.subset_span ?_))
  rw [Set.mem_ofPred_eq, ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_eq,
    isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_algebraMap]
  exact hstd

variable (n) in
/-- **Standard syntomic charts satisfy fpqc descent.** If `S` is faithfully flat over `R` and
`S ⊗[R] T` is locally standard syntomic of relative dimension `n` over `S`, then `T` is locally
standard syntomic of relative dimension `n` over `R`. -/
theorem codescendsAlong_locally_isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_faithfullyFlat :
    RingHom.CodescendsAlong (RingHom.Locally (IsStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension n))
      RingHom.FaithfullyFlat := by
  refine .mk _ (locally_isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_propertyIsLocal n).respectsIso
    fun R S T _ _ _ _ _ h h' ↦ ?_
  rw [RingHom.faithfullyFlat_algebraMap_iff] at h
  -- Flatness and finite presentation descend.
  have : Module.Flat S (S ⊗[R] T) :=
    RingHom.flat_algebraMap_iff.mp (flat_of_locally_isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension h')
  have : Algebra.FinitePresentation S (S ⊗[R] T) := RingHom.finitePresentation_algebraMap.mp
    (finitePresentation_of_locally_isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension h')
  have : Module.Flat R T := .of_flat_tensorProduct R T S
  have : Algebra.FinitePresentation R T := .of_finitePresentation_tensorProduct_of_faithfullyFlat S
  -- By the fibrewise criterion it suffices to treat the fibre over a prime `p` of `R`. Choose a
  -- prime `P` of `S` over `p`; the fibre of `S ⊗[R] T` over `P` is the base change of the fibre
  -- of `T` over `p` along the residue field extension `κ(p) → κ(P)`.
  refine locally_isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_of_fiber fun p _ ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨P, hP⟩ := PrimeSpectrum.comap_surjective_of_faithfullyFlat (A := R) (B := S)
    ⟨p, inferInstance⟩
  let K := P.asIdeal.ResidueField
  have hpK : RingHom.ker (algebraMap R K) = p := Ideal.ext fun r ↦ by
    rw [RingHom.mem_ker, IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply R S K,
      Ideal.algebraMap_residueField_eq_zero, ← Ideal.mem_comap, ← PrimeSpectrum.comap_asIdeal, hP]
  obtain ⟨_, _⟩ := Ideal.exists_algebra_residueField_isScalarTower p hpK
  have hK := (RingHom.locally_isStableUnderBaseChange
    (isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_respectsIso n)
    (isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_isStableUnderBaseChange n)).tensorProduct K h'
  let e : K ⊗[S] (S ⊗[R] T) ≃ₐ[K] K ⊗[p.ResidueField] p.Fiber T :=
    (Algebra.TensorProduct.cancelBaseChange R S K K T).trans
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.cancelBaseChange R p.ResidueField K K T).symm
  refine locally_isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_of_tensorProduct (K := K) ?_
  have hK' := (locally_isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_propertyIsLocal n).respectsIso.left
    (T := K ⊗[p.ResidueField] p.Fiber T) _ e.toRingEquiv hK
  have he : (e.toRingEquiv : _ →+* _).comp (algebraMap K (K ⊗[S] (S ⊗[R] T))) =
      algebraMap K (K ⊗[p.ResidueField] p.Fiber T) :=
    RingHom.ext fun x ↦ e.commutes x
  rw [← he]
  exact hK'

section Etale

variable {B : Type u} [CommRing B] [Algebra k B] [Algebra A B] [IsScalarTower k A B]

/-- Near a prime `q` of `A` under a prime of a flat, finitely presented, Noetherian `A`-algebra `B`
of Krull dimension at most `n`, every prime of `A` has height at most `n`: the image of
`Spec B → Spec A` is an open neighbourhood of `q`, and flat maps do not lower heights. -/
private theorem exists_notMem_forall_height_le_of_flat [Module.Flat A B]
    [Algebra.FinitePresentation A B] [IsNoetherianRing A] [IsNoetherianRing B]
    (hdim : ringKrullDim B ≤ n)
    (Q : Ideal B) [Q.IsPrime] :
    ∃ a ∉ Q.comap (algebraMap A B),
      ∀ p : Ideal A, p.IsPrime → a ∉ p → Ideal.height p ≤ n := by
  have hopen := PrimeSpectrum.isOpenMap_comap_of_hasGoingDown_of_finitePresentation
    (R := A) (S := B) _ isOpen_univ
  rw [Set.image_univ] at hopen
  obtain ⟨_, ⟨a, rfl⟩, ha, hle⟩ :=
    PrimeSpectrum.isTopologicalBasis_basic_opens.exists_subset_of_mem_open
      (Set.mem_range_self ⟨Q, inferInstance⟩) hopen
  refine ⟨a, ha, fun p hp hap ↦ ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨P, hP⟩ := hle (show ⟨p, hp⟩ ∈ PrimeSpectrum.basicOpen a from hap)
  have : P.asIdeal.LiesOver p := ⟨congrArg PrimeSpectrum.asIdeal hP.symm⟩
  have hPp := Ideal.height_eq_height_add_of_liesOver_of_hasGoingDown p P.asIdeal
  have hPn : (P.asIdeal.height : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤ n :=
    Ideal.height_le_ringKrullDim_of_isPrime.trans hdim
  exact (le_self_add.trans_eq hPp.symm).trans (WithBot.coe_le_coe.mp hPn)

/-- The case of `exists_notMem_isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_localization_away_of_etale`
where `B` is standard étale over `A` and standard syntomic over `k`. -/
private theorem exists_notMem_isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_of_isStandardEtale
    [Algebra.FiniteType k A] [Algebra.IsStandardEtale A B]
    [Algebra.IsStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension n k B] (Q : Ideal B) [Q.IsPrime] :
    ∃ g ∉ Q.comap (algebraMap A B),
      Algebra.IsStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension n k (Localization.Away g) := by
  have : Algebra.FinitePresentation k A :=
    (Algebra.FinitePresentation.of_finiteType (R := k)).mp ‹_›
  let P := Algebra.Presentation.ofFinitePresentation k A
  -- The point `F = κ(Q)`, with its algebra structures over `A` and `k[ι]`.
  let F := Q.ResidueField
  let : Algebra A F := ((algebraMap B F).comp (algebraMap A B)).toAlgebra
  let : Algebra P.Ring F := ((algebraMap A F).comp (algebraMap P.Ring A)).toAlgebra
  have : IsScalarTower A B F := .of_algebraMap_eq' rfl
  have : IsScalarTower P.Ring A F := .of_algebraMap_eq' rfl
  have hF (r : P.Ring) (hr : algebraMap P.Ring A r ∈ Q.comap (algebraMap A B)) :
      algebraMap P.Ring F r = 0 :=
    Ideal.algebraMap_residueField_eq_zero.mpr hr
  -- Compare the presentation of `B` through the standard étale coordinates with a standard
  -- syntomic presentation of `B`: the kernel of `P` needs at most `#ι - n` generators near `Q`.
  have hfin : Module.finrank F (F ⊗[P.Ring] P.ker) + n ≤
      Nat.card (Fin (Algebra.Presentation.ofFinitePresentationVars k A)) := by
    obtain ⟨ι', σ', _, _, P', hP'⟩ :=
      (‹Algebra.IsStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension n k B›).exists_presentation
    let Pe := (Algebra.IsStandardEtale.nonempty_standardEtalePresentation (R := A) (S := B)).some
    have : Module.Finite A P.toExtension.Cotangent := Algebra.Extension.Cotangent.finite P.fg_ker
    have h1 := (Pe.toSubmersivePresentation.toGenerators.comp P.toGenerators
      ).finrank_tensor_cotangent_add_card_le F P'
    rw [Algebra.Generators.finrank_tensor_cotangent_comp_of_isStandardEtale P.toGenerators
      Pe.toSubmersivePresentation F, P.toGenerators.finrank_tensor_cotangent F] at h1
    simp only [Nat.card_eq_fintype_card, Fintype.card_sum, Fintype.card_fin, hP'] at h1 ⊢
    omega
  have : Algebra.FinitePresentation k B := RingHom.finitePresentation_algebraMap.mp
    (isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_algebraMap (n := n) |>.mpr inferInstance
      ).finitePresentation
  have : IsNoetherianRing A := Algebra.FiniteType.isNoetherianRing k A
  have : IsNoetherianRing B := Algebra.FiniteType.isNoetherianRing k B
  obtain ⟨a, ha, hdim⟩ := exists_notMem_forall_height_le_of_flat (A := A)
    (ringKrullDim_le_of_locally_isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension (RingHom.locally_of
      (isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_respectsIso n) (algebraMap k B)
      (isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_algebraMap.mpr inferInstance))) Q
  exact exists_notMem_isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_localization_away_of_finrank_le
    P _ F hF hfin ha hdim

/-- **Local complete intersections descend along étale maps.** Let `A` be a finite type algebra
over a field `k`, and `B` an étale `A`-algebra which is locally standard syntomic of relative
dimension `n` over `k`. Then every prime of `A` under a prime `Q` of `B` has a neighbourhood
`A[1/g]` which is standard syntomic of relative dimension `n` over `k`. -/
theorem exists_notMem_isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_localization_away_of_etale
    [Algebra.FiniteType k A] [Algebra.Etale A B]
    (h : RingHom.Locally (IsStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension n) (algebraMap k B))
    (Q : Ideal B) [Q.IsPrime] :
    ∃ g ∉ Q.comap (algebraMap A B),
      Algebra.IsStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension n k (Localization.Away g) := by
  -- A standard étale neighbourhood `B₁ = B[1/t₁]` of `Q`, still locally standard syntomic.
  obtain ⟨t₁, ht₁, _⟩ := Algebra.IsEtaleAt.exists_isStandardEtale (R := A) Q
  let B₁ := Localization.Away t₁
  let Q₁ := Q.map (algebraMap B B₁)
  have : Q₁.IsPrime := IsLocalization.isPrime_of_isPrime_disjoint (.powers t₁) B₁ Q
    inferInstance ((Ideal.disjoint_powers_iff_notMem _ ‹Q.IsPrime›.isRadical).mpr ht₁)
  have h₁ : RingHom.Locally (IsStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension n) (algebraMap k B₁) := by
    rw [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_eq k B B₁]
    exact RingHom.locally_stableUnderCompositionWithLocalizationAwayTarget
      (isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_stableUnderCompositionWithLocalizationAway n).right
      _ t₁ _ h
  -- A standard syntomic neighbourhood `B₂ = B₁[1/t₂]` of `Q₁`, still standard étale.
  obtain ⟨s, hs, hst⟩ := h₁
  obtain ⟨t₂, hts, hdisj⟩ := Ideal.exists_disjoint_powers_of_span_eq_top s hs Q₁
    ‹Q₁.IsPrime›.ne_top
  let B₂ := Localization.Away t₂
  have : Algebra.IsStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension n k B₂ := by
    rw [← isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_algebraMap,
      IsScalarTower.algebraMap_eq k B₁ B₂]
    exact hst t₂ hts
  have : Algebra.IsStandardEtale A B₂ := .of_isLocalizationAway t₂
  let Q₂ := Q₁.map (algebraMap B₁ B₂)
  have : Q₂.IsPrime := IsLocalization.isPrime_of_isPrime_disjoint _ _ Q₁ inferInstance hdisj.symm
  have hQ : Q₂.comap (algebraMap A B₂) = Q.comap (algebraMap A B) := by
    have e₂ : Q₂.comap (algebraMap B₁ B₂) = Q₁ :=
      IsLocalization.under_map_of_isPrime_disjoint (.powers t₂) B₂ inferInstance hdisj.symm
    have e₁ : Q₁.comap (algebraMap B B₁) = Q :=
      IsLocalization.under_map_of_isPrime_disjoint (.powers t₁) B₁ inferInstance
        ((Ideal.disjoint_powers_iff_notMem _ ‹Q.IsPrime›.isRadical).mpr ht₁)
    rw [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_eq A B₁ B₂, IsScalarTower.algebraMap_eq A B B₁,
      ← Ideal.comap_comap, ← Ideal.comap_comap, e₂, e₁]
  rw [← hQ]
  exact exists_notMem_isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_of_isStandardEtale Q₂

/-- **Local complete intersections descend along étale covers.** Let `A` be a finite type algebra
over a field `k`, and `B` a faithfully flat étale `A`-algebra. If `B` is locally standard syntomic
of relative dimension `n` over `k`, then so is `A`. -/
theorem locally_isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_of_etale [Algebra.FiniteType k A]
    [Algebra.Etale A B] [Module.FaithfullyFlat A B]
    (h : RingHom.Locally (IsStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension n) (algebraMap k B)) :
    RingHom.Locally (IsStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension n) (algebraMap k A) := by
  rw [RingHom.locally_iff_span_eq_top]
  by_contra hne
  obtain ⟨m, hm, hle⟩ := Ideal.exists_le_maximal _ hne
  obtain ⟨Q, hQ⟩ := PrimeSpectrum.comap_surjective_of_faithfullyFlat (A := A) (B := B)
    ⟨m, hm.isPrime⟩
  obtain ⟨g, hg, hstd⟩ :=
    exists_notMem_isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_localization_away_of_etale (A := A) h
      Q.asIdeal
  rw [show Q.asIdeal.comap (algebraMap A B) = m from congrArg PrimeSpectrum.asIdeal hQ] at hg
  refine hg (hle (Ideal.subset_span ?_))
  rw [Set.mem_ofPred_eq, ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_eq,
    isStandardSyntomicOfRelativeDimension_algebraMap]
  exact hstd

